    "created_at": "2026-05-19T06:28:13Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-05-19T06:28:13Z",
    "body": "8288 doesn't define a parsing algorithm, and ABNF sucks for parsing. In HTTP clients are [allowed to take reasonable steps to recover values](https://httpwg.org/specs/rfc9110.html#error.handling), so technically this is ok, but of course that's pretty unsatisfying.\n\nIf someone can suggest reasonable ABNF we could file that as a technical errata to the spec; the outcome would likely be HOLD FOR UPDATE but at least it'd be recorded.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
